1
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Born into poverty. Destined for stardom. He lived the American dream.

2
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
La Bamba is a drama, music film directed by Luis Valdez.

3
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Los Angeles teenager Ritchie Valens becomes an overnight rock 'n' roll success in 1958,
thanks to a love ballad called "Donna" that he wrote for his girlfriend.

4
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
But as his star rises, Valens has conflicts with his jealous brother, Bob, and becomes haunted by a recurring
nightmare of a plane crash just as he begins his first national tour alongside Buddy Holly.

5
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Ritchie Valens, played by Lou Diamond Phillips.

6
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Donna Ludwig, played by Danielle von Zerneck.

7
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Rosie Morales, played by Elizabeth Peña.

8
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Connie Valenzuela, played by Rosanna DeSoto.

9
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:42,000
Bob Morales, played by Esai Morales.

10
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Bob Keane, played by Joe Pantoliano.

11
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
La Bamba is a 1987 American biographical drama film
written and directed by Luis Valdez.

12
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:54,000
The film follows the life and short-lived musical career of
American Chicano rock and roll star Ritchie Valens.

13
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
The film stars Lou Diamond Phillips as Valens, Esai Morales, Rosanna
DeSoto, Elizabeth Peña, Danielle von Zerneck and Joe Pantoliano.

14
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
The film also covers the effect that Valens' career had on the lives of his half-brother
Bob Morales, his girlfriend Donna Ludwig, and the rest of his family.

15
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film is titled after a traditional Mexican folk song of the same name,
which Valens transformed into a rock and roll rendition in 1958.

16
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
In 2017, La Bamba was included in the annual selection of 25 motion
pictures added to the National Film Registry of the U.S.

17
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
Library of Congress being deemed "culturally, historically, or
aesthetically significant" and recommended for preservation.

18
01:37:12,000 --> 01:37:18,000
The film explores themes of rock 'n' roll,
biography, death, dying young, nostalgic.

19
01:42:36,000 --> 01:42:42,000
The tone is emotional.
